	(text_box "WHY THE 74LVC1GU04\nU = UNBUFFERED, one gain stage.  A buffered\ninverter is three cascaded stages, and three\npoles inside a feedback loop oscillate; one\npole cannot.  That is what makes the 1M\nself-bias safe here.\nLVC = 5.5 V tolerant inputs on a 3.3 V rail\n(there is no clamp diode to Vcc), so a 5 V\nsource survives contact.\nIt also has no input slew-rate limit in its\nRecommended Operating Conditions - unlike\nthe buffered G04 - because it is meant to be\nrun in its linear region."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 134.6200 166.3700 0)
		(size 62.2300 36.8300)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 220 235 255 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.4000 1.4000)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d6f8144a-5eb0-01f3-bed0-9d515c75a15b")
	)
	(text_box "AT THE GATE, at TP_SQ\n1.64 Vpp, center 1.65 V\n0.83 to 2.47 V\nslew ~820 mV/ns"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 172.7200 78.7400 0)
		(size 46.9900 12.7000)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
