	(text "out:  PPS_03, one rising edge per second, 0/3.3 V, straight to the RPi header"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 288.2900 323.8500 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5000 1.5000)
				(italic yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "3387e0ff-d59f-728d-c3fd-9c0565a1561e")
	)
	(text_box "DC-COUPLED, DELIBERATELY.\nThe pps widths in this inventory span 1 us (FE-5680A) to 100 ms (ZED-F9T,\nLBE-1421), and no single AC-coupling RC covers five decades: a 10n/100k network\npasses the 1 us pulse and droops away to nothing 1% into the 100 ms one.\nThe 1k/10k divider is fitted on EVERY pps channel and suits a 3.3 V and a 5 V\nsource alike: 3.00 V and 4.55 V at the gate, both comfortably above the\nSchmitt's VT+ and below its 5.5 V recommended maximum.  74LVC inputs are 5 V\ntolerant on a 3.3 V rail, so the divider is there to keep the swing sane rather\nthan merely survivable -- and to keep every channel identically populated."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.2400 358.1400 0)
		(size 121.9200 26.6700)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 245 210 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.4000 1.4000)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "97a8a901-2930-e5eb-f4ec-6620dc0142e8")
	)
	(text_box "SCHMITT BUFFER, NOT AN INVERTER.\nHysteresis is wrong for the 10 MHz path - it moves the trigger off the zero\ncrossing and turns amplitude into phase - but it is right here: a pps is a rare,\nfast, possibly noisy edge on a long cable, which is the chatter case hysteresis\nexists for.\nNo self-bias: a Schmitt sets its own thresholds and must not be biased into its\nown linear region.\nTimed in the FPGA's 200.02 MHz domain to 5 ns, far below every GPSDO's own\nsawtooth."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 144.7800 358.1400 0)
		(size 121.9200 26.6700)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
